        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2011 Military Bowl, 2011–12 NCAA bowl season\n- Places: Robert F. Kennedy Memorial Stadium, Washington, D.C.\n- Organizations: U.S. men's national soccer team\n- Teams: 2011 Toledo Rockets football team, Air Force\n\nFacts:\n- The 2011 Military Bowl Presented by Northrop Grumman was the fourth edition of the game.\n- The 2011 Military Bowl was a post-season American college football bowl game held on December 28, 2011.\n- The 2011 Military Bowl was played at Robert F. Kennedy Memorial Stadium in Washington, D.C. as part of the 2011–12 NCAA bowl season.\n- The U.S. men's national soccer team played 22 matches at Robert F. Kennedy Memorial Stadium from 1977 to 2013, more than at any other stadium.\n- The 2011 Toledo Rockets football team was invited to the Military Bowl.\n- The 2011 Toledo Rockets football team defeated Air Force 42–41 in the Military Bowl.",
